    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nbase16\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nNeogit applies its own highlighting, which happens to conflict with Mini's base16 module. This becomes noticeable in certain instances, such as the diffview, where red markers are displayed with a black foreground. I discovered that modifying nvim's colorscheme after opening Neogit results in colors being completely absent - I believe that Mini is likely overriding highlights that Neogit relies upon? \r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.9.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. `nvim`\r\n2. `Neogit`\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nreturn {\r\n  \"CKolkey/neogit\",\r\n  cmd = 'Neogit',\r\n  dependencies = {\r\n    \"nvim-lua/plenary.nvim\",\r\n    \"sindrets/diffview.nvim\"\r\n  },\r\n  keys = {\r\n    { \"<Leader>ng\", \"<cmd>Neogit<CR>\", desc = \"Toggle Neogit\" }\r\n  },\r\n  opts = {\r\n    integrations = {\r\n      diffview = true\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nProper highlighting with Neogit, particularly in/with its diffview markers.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/f79248c7-3599-441d-b6cb-21eac09265ff)\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/e279507b-9011-45a8-adab-bcd0aaedcfb3)\r\n",
