        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Soooo... @CKolkey, I've looked into updating 'mini.base16' and 'mini.hues' to work with 'NeogitOrg/neogit'. Here are the results:\r\n\r\n- I've pushed updates for both color scheme modules with what seems like reasonable choices, as 'mini.hues' doesn't yet work (see below). \r\n- I found it extremely hard to understand which highlight group I need to update in order to change certain UI elements. Having some centralized table with this information might help here (hence NeogitOrg/neogit#627).\r\n- 'mini.hues' doesn't load because Neogit's `make_palette()` function makes assumptions about present attributes of certain highlight groups. For example, 'mini.hues' doesn't have foreground in 'Error' highlight group which [this line assumes](https://github.com/NeogitOrg/neogit/blob/bd7203e1f18ed72d1450688075f4d8f0b1c4f024/lua/neogit/lib/hl.lua#L137). Using NeogitOrg/neogit#617 makes it load with decent colors though.\r\n    I would like to give one piece of advice: the most robust approach to defining default highlight inside plugin is usually linking it to some built-in highlight group. This can be achieved with something like `nvim_set_hl(0, 'MyGroup', { default = true, link = 'Error' })`. Yes, it will probably result into less variation without dedicated color scheme support, but it will work for most cases. And will probably save you from all the new issues resulting from particular loading order of plugins.",
